THIRD-PARTY DATA ATTRIBUTION
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This project evaluates against the eTour traceability dataset.

eTour originates with the Center of Excellence for Software & Systems
Traceability (CoEST), and has been used extensively in requirements-traceability
research. Credit for the corpus belongs to its original authors.

The packaged form used here was obtained from:

    finegrained-traceability (FTLR)
    https://github.com/tobhey/finegrained-traceability
    Tobias Hey et al.
    Licensed under GPL-3.0

SCOPE OF USE

This project uses DATA from the FTLR repository only. No source code from that
repository has been copied into, adapted for, or incorporated into this project.

This distinction is deliberate and load-bearing. FTLR is licensed under GPL-3.0,
a copyleft license; this project is licensed under Apache-2.0, a permissive
license. Incorporating GPL-3.0 source into an Apache-2.0 project would create a
license conflict. Reading published work for ideas is ordinary scholarship and
is not restricted by either license; copying implementation is, and we do not.

The dataset itself is not redistributed as part of this repository. The `data/`
directory is excluded from version control, and the README documents how to
obtain the corpus from its original source. Users who fetch the eTour dataset do
so directly from the FTLR repository and are subject to its terms.
